{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>וְהָיְתָה שַׁבַּת וגו׳</b>. The meaning is: do not say that its rule will be like the rest of the table of the Most High, from which the priests partake; rather, ״לָכֶם״ — for all of you equally, priests, Levites, Israelites, and so on. And He returned and specified ״לְךָ״ and so on. Now if you say: if so, why was ״לָכֶם״ stated — should He not have said only ״הָאָרֶץ לְאָכְלָה לְךָ״ and so on? It would appear that He was careful to speak in this manner, for I would have said that the one mentioned earlier in the verse takes precedence in eating, in the manner they said (Sifrei): עֲנִיֶּיךָ וַעֲנִיֵּי עִירְךָ — your poor take precedence over the poor of your city, from what the verse states (Deuteronomy 15:7) ״כִּי יִהְיֶה בְךָ אֶבְיוֹן״ and so on. Therefore Scripture preempted and included them all together and said ״לָכֶם״, teaching that there is no barrier for one over another regarding the produce of the Sabbatical year."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:00:56.947119899Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}